POST /authz/v1/authorize — request<pre><code>{
  "requestId": "hive-access-request",
  "user":      { "name": "gary.adams", "groups": [ "fte", "mktg" ], "roles": [ "analyst" ] },
  "access": {
    "resource":    { "name": "table:default/sales", "attributes": { "OWNER": "nancy.boxer" } },
    "action":      "QUERY",
    "permissions": [ "select" ]
  },
  "context": {
    "serviceType":     "hive",
    "serviceName":     "dev_hive",
    "accessTime":      1755543894,
    "clientIpAddress": "172.16.45.59",
    "additionalInfo":  { "clientType": "beeline", "clusterName": "cl1" }
  }
}
</code></pre> response<pre><code>{
  "requestId": "hive-access-request",
  "decision":  "ALLOW",
  "permissions": {
    "select": {
      "access":    { "decision": "ALLOW", "policy": { "id": 1, "version": 1 } },
      "rowFilter": { "filterExpr": "dept = 'mktg'", "policy": { "id": 11, "version": 3 } }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

Evaluator Values Matches when <code>RangerScriptConditionEvaluator</code> A single script The script evaluates to <code>true</code>. See Script conditions. <code>RangerScriptTemplateConditionEvaluator</code> <code>yes</code>/<code>true</code> or <code>no</code>/<code>false</code> The script in the <code>scriptTemplate</code> option evaluates to <code>true</code>; <code>no</code>/<code>false</code> inverts the result. <p>Both script evaluators accept the option <code>enableJsonCtx</code>. The shipped definitions also set <code>engineName</code> to <code>JavaScript</code>; JavaScript is the only engine <code>ScriptEngineUtil</code> creates. The <code>tag</code> service definition uses the template evaluator for <code>accessed-after-expiry</code>.</p> <p>Notes:</p> <ul> <li>Cluster name and type come from the plugin configuration:   <code>ranger.plugin.&lt;serviceType&gt;.access.cluster.name</code> and <code>ranger.plugin.&lt;serviceType&gt;.access.cluster.type</code>   (<code>RangerPluginConfig</code>).   They are also available to scripts as <code>REQ.clusterName</code> and <code>REQ.clusterType</code>.</li> <li>The tag-presence evaluators read the tags added by <code>RangerTagEnricher</code>, so they only work in   services linked to a tag service.</li> <li>The Hive "accessed together" evaluators rely on the Hive plugin recording every resource referenced   by a query in the request context (<code>REQUESTED_RESOURCES</code>).</li> </ul> <p>An example declaring the IP and time-of-day conditions for Kafka (<code>ip-range</code> already exists in the shipped definition):</p> <pre><code>"policyConditions": [
  {
    "itemId": 1,
    "name": "ip-range",
    "evaluator": "org.apache.ranger.plugin.conditionevaluator.RangerIpMatcher",
    "label": "IP Address Range",
    "description": "IP Address Range",
    "uiHint": "{ \"isMultiValue\":true }"
  },
  {
    "itemId": 2,
    "name": "time-of-day",
    "evaluator": "org.apache.ranger.plugin.conditionevaluator.RangerTimeOfDayMatcher",
    "label": "Time of day",
    "description": "Ranges such as 9am-5pm",
    "uiHint": "{ \"isMultiValue\":true }"
  }
]
</code></pre> <p>And a Kafka policy item that uses both:</p> <pre><code>{
  "accesses": [ { "type": "publish", "isAllowed": true } ],
  "groups": ["ingest"],
  "conditions": [
    { "type": "ip-range",    "values": ["10.20.*", "192.168.1.100"] },
    { "type": "time-of-day", "values": ["6am-8pm"] }
  ],
  "delegateAdmin": false
}
</code></pre>

ranger-hive-audit.xml<pre><code>&lt;configuration&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.is.enabled&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;

  &lt;!-- searchable store for the Admin UI --&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr.zookeepers&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;zk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181/ranger_audits&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr.batch.filespool.dir&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;/var/log/hive/audit/solr/spool&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;

  &lt;!-- long-term archive --&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.hdfs&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.hdfs.dir&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;hdfs://nn.example.com:8020/ranger/audit&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.hdfs.batch.filespool.dir&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;/var/log/hive/audit/hdfs/spool&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;

  &lt;!-- collapse repeated identical events --&gt;
  &lt;property&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.provider.summary.enabled&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>

ranger-&lt;component&gt;-audit.xml<pre><code>&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr.zookeepers&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;zk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181/ranger_audits&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.solr.batch.filespool.dir&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;/var/log/hive/audit/solr/spool&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
</code></pre> <p>For a standalone Solr, set <code>xasecure.audit.destination.solr.urls</code> (for example <code>http://solr.example.com:6083/solr/ranger_audits</code>) instead of <code>zookeepers</code>.</p> <p>For a Kerberized Solr, either point the JVM's <code>java.security.auth.login.config</code> at a JAAS file, or set <code>xasecure.audit.destination.solr.force.use.inmemory.jaas.config=true</code> and supply the login module through the <code>xasecure.audit.jaas.Client.*</code> properties. For HTTPS the plugin's <code>xasecure.policymgr.clientssl.*</code> truststore (and keystore, for mutual TLS) settings are reused. All keys are listed in Audit framework.</p>

Key Default Type Description <code>ranger.audit.solr.zookeepers</code> (none) String ZooKeeper connect string (SolrCloud); takes precedence over <code>ranger.audit.solr.urls</code>. <code>ranger.audit.solr.urls</code> (none) List Collection URL for standalone Solr, for example <code>http://solr.example.com:6083/solr/ranger_audits</code>. <code>ranger.audit.solr.collection.name</code> <code>ranger_audits</code> String Collection to query, with <code>zookeepers</code>. <code>ranger.solr.audit.user</code> (none) String User for Solr basic authentication. <code>ranger.solr.audit.user.password</code> (none) Password Password for Solr basic authentication. ranger-admin-site.xml<pre><code>&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;ranger.audit.source.type&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;solr&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;ranger.audit.solr.zookeepers&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;zk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181/ranger_audits&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The docker stack (<code>--profile audit-store-solr</code>) runs a <code>ranger-solr</code> container with a <code>ranger_audits</code> configset from <code>dev-support/ranger-docker/scripts/solr/solr-ranger_audits</code>, protected by the Ranger Solr plugin.</p>

ranger-&lt;component&gt;-audit.xml<pre><code>&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.urls&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;os1.example.com,os2.example.com&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.protocol&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;https&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.authentication.type&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;basic&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.user&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;ranger&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.password&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;secret&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.opensearch.batch.filespool.dir&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;/var/log/hive/audit/opensearch/spool&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>port</code> defaults to <code>9200</code> and <code>index</code> to <code>ranger_audits</code>. Use <code>authentication.type=kerberos</code> with <code>kerberos.principal</code> and <code>kerberos.keytab</code> for SPNEGO. All keys are listed in Audit framework.</p>

ranger-&lt;component&gt;-audit.xml<pre><code>&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.elasticsearch&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;true&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.elasticsearch.urls&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;es1.example.com,es2.example.com&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.elasticsearch.protocol&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;https&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.elasticsearch.user&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;ranger&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
&lt;property&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;xasecure.audit.destination.elasticsearch.password&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value&gt;secret&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>port</code> defaults to <code>9200</code> and <code>index</code> to <code>ranger_audits</code>. If <code>password</code> is the path of an existing keytab file, the client authenticates with SPNEGO using <code>user</code> as the principal. All keys are listed in Audit framework.</p>
